+# mtk/mt6895/soc.conf: the MediaTek MT6895 (Dimensity 8100 / 8000), whatever phone it is in. A phone with this SoC says
+# `soc mt6895` in its device.conf and includes configs/mt6895.config from its defconfig. docs/porting/repositories.md has
+# every word; mtk/README.md says what the MediaTek part of this tree is.
+#
+# "mt6895" is what the device tree calls it: the live tree of the first phone (xaga) has mt6895.dts as its board and every
+# node is `mediatek,mt6895-<block>`. The SoC is sold as the Dimensity 8100 (MT6895) and the Dimensity 8000 (MT6895Z); the
+# two differ in clocks, not in addresses, so one layer holds both and the phone's device.conf picks the clocks.
+
+soc mt6895
+	title       MediaTek MT6895 family (Dimensity 8100, Dimensity 8000)
+	vendor      MediaTek
+	cores       8: four Cortex-A55 (cores 0-3) and four Cortex-A78 (cores 4-7)
+	gpu         Mali-G610 (Valhall, "arm,mali-valhall" in the device tree at 0x13000000)
+	maintainer  the HakiOS developers (mtk/README.md)
